<section>
    <p class="eyebrow">ROCKFORD POLICE DEPARTMENT</p>
    <h2>Flock, Axon, cameras, analytics, and gunshot detection</h2>
    <div class="finding_grid">
      <article>
        <span class="status_label">DOCUMENTED</span>
        <h3>2026 Flock contract</h3>
        <p>Rockford approved a $443,998.16 sole-source Flock contract in 2026. The city's supporting memorandum says earlier retail-crime grants funded Flock Operating System software, Flock license-plate readers, and Flock PTZ cameras for the Police Department Intelligence Unit.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="status_label">DOCUMENTED</span>
        <h3>150+ mobile and stationary LPRs</h3>
        <p>Rockford's crime-reduction page states the city purchased more than 150 mobile and stationary license-plate readers.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="status_label">DOCUMENTED</span>
        <h3>Axon body-worn cameras</h3>
        <p>Rockford's body-camera policy requires recordings to be uploaded through AXON docking stations and stored in a secure web-based digital-media system.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="status_label">DOCUMENTED</span>
        <h3>Six drones / eight reported flights</h3>
        <p>The SFY 2024 statewide drone report records six Rockford Police Department drones and eight flights during the reporting period.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="status_label">DOCUMENTED</span>
        <h3>Fixed cameras</h3>
        <p>The city reports that it quadrupled the number of cameras in high-traffic and high-crime areas.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="status_label">DOCUMENTED</span>
        <h3>Gunshot-detection software</h3>
        <p>Rockford lists gunshot-detection software among its enforcement technology. A 2022 City Council action also approved a Flock package containing gunshot detection and 64 license-plate readers.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="status_label">DOCUMENTED</span>
        <h3>Social-media analytics</h3>
        <p>The city states it instituted social-analytic software to track criminal use of social media. The current public page does not identify the vendor or product.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="status_label">DOCUMENTED</span>
        <h3>Flock renewal funding continues</h3>
        <p>A 2026 grant action states FY2027 organized-retail-crime funding will partially cover annual subscription fees for Flock Safety License Plate Reader Video Wing Enhanced.</p>
      </article>
    </div>

